  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have a simple \"Audio Source\" in the world that plays a wave file.  With the \"Enable Spatialization\" box checked in the \"VRC_SpatialAudioSource\" component, the sound becomes distorted and crackly.\nVideo of the problem: https://youtu.be/98uCAn1CIrM\nNote how when the box is checked: 1) the sound changes from pulsing to a steady tone; 2) crackling is present.\nI have tried changing all the parameters I could think of: 44.1kHz and 48kHz sampling rates for the source wave file; disabling compression when importing the wave file asset; reducing the volume in the file to 50%; all the various settings in the Audio Source and VRC_SpatialAudioSource components.  Nothing has made a difference.\nThe audio file in question is available here (345 kB) https://mrzebra.co.uk/stuff/Binaural%20Beats%20110.5%20and%20111.5%20Hz.wav",
